/-!
# Structurality from `Equation4517` through a two-guard companion

Generated by `defwork/itautcell2.py`.  `Equation4517` is `x ◇ (y ◇ z) = (x ◇ z) ◇ w`.  Its guarded obligation
-- a bijection of a finite model commuting with `x □ y = if (M.op a b) = a then (M.op b b) else if (M.op b a) = (M.op b b) then b else (M.op b a)` is an automorphism of `◇` --
is `GuardAut2_pxy_x_pyx_pyy_pyy_y_pyx_Equation4517`, proved elsewhere.  That obligation names no target, so every
law the companion satisfies is another cell for free, and there
are 3 of them below.
-/

